WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.351
<v Examiner>Scenario three.

2
00:00:02.351 --> 00:00:06.620
<v Examiner>Mr Tane is sixty-four, on the surgical ward after a bowel resection.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.942
<v Examiner>He has angina and uses a G T N spray.

4
00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:13.775
<v Examiner>He's prescribed morphine two point five milligrams I V P R N for severe pain,

5
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:18.545
<v Examiner>and his own G T N spray, four hundred micrograms, one spray S L, sublingual,

6
00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:19.863
<v Examiner>P R N for chest pain.

7
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:20.923
<v Examiner>Two marks.

8
00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:22.753
<v Examiner>Morphine is a controlled drug.

9
00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:27.695
<v Examiner>What is a controlled drug, and give one way it's handled differently on the ward.

10
00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:32.308
A controlled drug is a medicine under special legal controls,

11
00:00:32.308 --> 00:00:36.608
under the Misuse of Drugs Act 1975, to reduce misuse and abuse.

12
00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:38.588
That's her formative two key.

13
00:00:38.588 --> 00:00:44.594
On the ward it's kept in a double-locked safe, recorded in the controlled drug register,

14
00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:47.120
and checked and signed by two nurses.

15
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.259
Remember: every controlled drug is prescribed,

16
00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:53.263
but not every prescribed drug is controlled.

17
00:00:53.713 --> 00:00:54.372
<v Examiner>Two marks.

18
00:00:54.372 --> 00:00:58.918
<v Examiner>Identify two things the nurse monitors after giving Mr Tane morphine.

19
00:00:59.368 --> 00:01:02.440
His respiratory rate and his level of sedation,

20
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.231
because respiratory depression is morphine's toxic effect.

21
00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:08.845
And his pain score, to see if it worked.

22
00:01:08.845 --> 00:01:12.701
You could also say blood pressure, nausea, or constipation.

23
00:01:13.151 --> 00:01:13.828
<v Examiner>Two marks.

24
00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:17.887
<v Examiner>Why is G T N given sublingually, and what's one side effect?

25
00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:22.162
Under the tongue, it's absorbed straight into the bloodstream,

26
00:01:22.162 --> 00:01:26.726
so it works very fast and it skips the first-pass metabolism in the liver.

27
00:01:26.726 --> 00:01:31.352
Angina is dangerous: the heart muscle is short of oxygen, so speed matters.

28
00:01:31.352 --> 00:01:34.930
A side effect: headache, dizziness, or low blood pressure,

29
00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.644
which is why he sits down before he uses it.

30
00:01:38.094 --> 00:01:38.658
<v Examiner>One mark.

31
00:01:38.658 --> 00:01:41.350
<v Examiner>Mr Tane says he doesn't want his next dose.

32
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.915
<v Examiner>What should the nurse do?

33
00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:46.867
Respect it: a person can legally refuse a medicine.

34
00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:51.742
Find out why, document the refusal, and tell the R N or the prescriber.

35
00:01:51.742 --> 00:01:55.312
True, and document it, was her formative one answer.

36
00:01:55.762 --> 00:01:57.475
Scenario three, Mr Tane.

37
00:01:57.475 --> 00:02:02.686
Controlled drug: under special legal controls to reduce misuse and abuse;

38
00:02:02.686 --> 00:02:05.613
double-locked safe, register, two nurses.

39
00:02:05.613 --> 00:02:09.896
After morphine, monitor respiratory rate, sedation and pain.

40
00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:16.035
G T N is sublingual for speed and to skip first-pass; headache and low blood pressure,

41
00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:16.892
so sit down.

42
00:02:16.892 --> 00:02:20.389
A refusal: respect it, ask why, document, report.
